[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-3ba49a21-72d3-4607-b242-3479eaec0866\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Fri 17 Apr 2026 17:00 - 17:15 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2026/icse-2026-venue-asia-i\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Asia I</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">AI for Software Engineering 26</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/jiakunliu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Jiakun Liu</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"3ba49a21-72d3-4607-b242-3479eaec0866\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Enhancing LLM Code Generation with Ensembles: A Similarity-Based Selection Approach</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Ensemble learning has been widely used in machine learning to improve model robustness, accuracy, and generalization, but has not yet been applied to code generation tasks with large language models (LLMs). We propose an ensemble approach for LLMs in code generation. Instead of relying on the output of a single model, we generate multiple candidate programs from different LLMs and apply a structured voting mechanism to select the most reliable solution. For voting, we compute syntactic and semantic similarity using CodeBLEU and behavioral equivalence using CrossHair\u2019s differential behavior analysis. By aggregating these similarity scores, we select the program that best aligns with the consensus among the candidates. We show through experiments that our ensemble approach consistently outperforms standalone LLMs on the well-known HumanEval and the more challenging LiveCodeBench datasets, achieving an accuracy of 90.2% and 50.2%, respectively, on the two datasets. In comparison, the best-performing LLM (GPT-4o) has an accuracy of 83.5% and 43.4%, respectively. Furthermore, even when restricted to free open source models, our method achieves an accuracy of 80.5% and 41.6%, respectively, demonstrating the viability of our approach in resource-constrained settings.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/tarekmahmud\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Tarek Mahmud\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/tarekmahmud/ee18d789-bbfa-4881-a94b-a139e16a52ad/micro-avatar?1783979918000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Tarek Mahmud<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Texas State University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Bangladesh</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/binduan\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Bin Duan\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/binduan/a5fe3def-0b96-4644-8152-f4101b265b79/micro-avatar?1783972214000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Bin Duan<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of Queensland</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/corinapasareanu1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Corina S. <span class=\"name-visual-sep\"></span>P\u0103s\u0103reanu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Carnegie Mellon University; NASA Ames</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/guoweiyang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Guowei Yang\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/guoweiyang/20741d4a-9474-40e7-a21c-359f005e7190/micro-avatar?1784121929000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Guowei Yang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of Queensland</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Australia</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/101/Enhancing-LLM-Code-Generation-with-Ensembles-A-Similarity-Based-Selection-Approach\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-3ba49a21-72d3-4607-b242-3479eaec0866').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show